 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_5activj",
   "entryDay": 38,
   "cause": "the arena",
   "lines": [
    "d38: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Felicia Diaz is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d38: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d38: 🕯️ Felicia Diaz is dead — the arena. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d38: What Felicia kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d38: \"Felicia's gone.\" Priya looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Felicia.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d38: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Dwayne blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Debris Shelter (Level 1). A lean-to of branches and leaves beats nothing. Dead air is insulation.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Reading Tracks (Level 1). Fresh tracks have sharp edges. Old tracks crumble. You can tell how recently something passed.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Wire Snares (Level 1). A loop of wire on a game trail. Simple, effective, ancient. Check at dawn.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Cordage (Level 1). Twist plant fibers into string. Dogbane, nettle, yucca — strong fibers are everywhere.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Field Dressing (Level 1). Break down game fast and clean. Less waste, more meat, usable parts.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Animal Behavior (Level 1). Most animals flee. Give them an escape route and they take it. Cornered animals fight.",
    "d38: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d38: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Felicia Diaz, 38 days. The mantle passes to Dwayne Patel.",
    "d38: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Dwayne Patel, 41 — a trail crew lead. Their hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Echo Location, Berserker Rage.",
    "d38: The village's quarrel was with Felicia — and Felicia is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d38: At the grave, Trong, Rewi, Somchai and 3 more speak for Dwayne — \"Felicia trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d38: The fire knew Dwayne before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_agk4pzy",
   "entryDay": 38,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d38: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Dwayne Patel is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d38: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d38: 🕯️ Dwayne Patel is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d38: What Dwayne kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d38: \"Dwayne's gone.\" Priya looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Dwayne.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d38: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Trong blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d38: 📖 LEARNED: Tireless Stride (Level 1). You walk like water downhill — no wasted steps, no wasted breath. Every mile costs 15% less.",
    "d38: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d38: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Dwayne Patel, 38 days. The mantle passes to Trong Binh.",
    "d38: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Trong Binh, 69 — a postal worker. Their hands know different work now: Beast-calm, Bloodhound.",
    "d38: You knew Dwayne — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d38: At the grave, Rewi, Somchai, Ivy and 2 more speak for Trong — \"Dwayne trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d38: The fire knew Trong before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "deadId": "gen_qsijsk6",
   "entryDay": 72,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d72: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Trong Binh is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d72: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d72: 🕯️ Trong Binh is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d72: What Trong kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d72: \"Trong's gone.\" Priya looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Trong.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d72: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Somchai blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d72: ★ The record corrects itself: this was never Maypop — it's Jackfruit. someone taught you wrong (their own memory). (The Codex marks the disagreement. You can call them out in conversation.)",
    "d72: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d72: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Trong Binh, 72 days. The mantle passes to Somchai Prasert.",
    "d72: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Somchai Prasert, 28 — a bike messenger. His hands know different work now: Bloodhound, Bird Whisperer, Trophy Room, Lucky Rock, Scream Cheese.",
    "d72: ◈ The System updates its file: the new bearer <redacted> \"Stalker of the Apex Predator.\" It had a word for this one before the Codex came.",
    "d72: The village's quarrel was with Trong — and Trong is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
    "d72: You knew Trong — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting them, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d72: At the grave, Rewi, Elena, Ivy and 3 more speak for Somchai — \"Trong trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d72: The fire knew Somchai before the Codex did — his name already carried weight here."
   ]
