   "lines": [
    "d77: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Priya Nair is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d77: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d77: 🕯️ Priya Nair is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d77: What Priya kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d77: \"Priya's gone.\" Elena looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Priya.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d77: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Rewi blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d77: 📖 LEARNED: Wound Care (Level 1). Clean it, close it, cover it. Pressure stops bleeding. Clean water is better than dirty hands.",
    "d77: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Precise Mend! Your healing knows where to go. +50% effectiveness. (Your knowledge of Wound Care amplifies your field_medicine.)",
    "d77: 📖 LEARNED: Food Preservation (Level 1). Salt, smoke, dry. The big three. Salt draws water out; bacteria can't live without it.",
    "d77: 📖 LEARNED: Herbal Medicine (Level 1). Willow bark = aspirin. Yarrow stops bleeding. Plantain draws out infection. The pharmacy is outside.",
    "d77: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d77: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Priya Nair, 77 days. The mantle passes to Rewi Tait.",
    "d77: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Rewi Tait, 59 — a Veterinarian. Their hands know different work now: Iron Stomach, Purify, Battlefield Grace, War Cry.",
    "d77: You knew Priya — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting her, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)",
    "d77: At the grave, Elena, Ivy, Miguel and 1 more speak for Rewi — \"Priya trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens.",
    "d77: The fire knew Rewi before the Codex did — their name already carried weight here."
   ]
